f 1072 #uuid "e9404e17-b865-57fd-909a-78dee18906a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425379 #edb/ref 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{x}{2}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{e}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1045 "Expected Values of Continuous Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186436284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436255 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ef1cf134-d58c-50a9-859d-b58621f65432" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436256 #edb/ref 1080 "2.87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436256 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175921860